# Backend Architecture

- Keep handlers thin. Route Telegram and HTTP work through services, repositories, validators, and router/provider abstractions already present in the repo.
- Use Alembic migrations for schema changes. Do not reintroduce startup `create_all()` schema creation.
- Preserve user isolation in every repository, search, memory, card, feedback, export, deletion, and admin path.
- Keep provider access behind the existing LLM router/provider layer. Do not call OpenAI, Gemini, OpenRouter, or Groq directly from handlers.
- Use structured parsers and typed models when possible instead of ad hoc string manipulation.
- Keep Redis Streams document jobs idempotent and observable. Do not store raw uploaded content longer than the documented private-beta policy allows.
- Update tests when changing security, privacy, quota, prompt, safety, router, validator, migration, or worker behavior.

## Useful Checks

```powershell
python -m ruff check .
python -m pytest -q
alembic upgrade head
```
